In 2019, Huang et al. significantly contributed to studies regarding the regioisomeric control of MOF functional groups and their chemical stabilities. Zr-based UiO-67 MOFs were selected as model MOFs, where a trifluoromethyl \(\left(\mathsf{C F}_{3}\right)\) group was regioisomerically

introduced onto the ligands to confirm its effects (Fig. 14) [47]. UiO-67-ortho- \(2\mathrm{CF}_{3}\) was obtained from the solvothermal reaction between \(Z\mathrm{r}C1_{4}\) and \(3,3^{\prime}\) -bis(trifluoromethyl)- \(\cdot4{,}4^{\prime}\) -biphenyldicar boxylic acid \((\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{BPDC}{-}c{-}2\mathrm{CF}_{3})\) and its regioisomer, UiO-67-meta\(2{\mathrm{CF}}_{3}\) , was synthesized using \(^{2,2^{\prime}}\) -bis(trifluoromethyl)- \(\cdot4{,}4^{\prime}\) -biphenyldicarboxylic acid \((\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{BPDC}{-}m{-}2\mathrm{CF}_{3})\) . While both regioisomers showed almost identical, pristine UiO-67 frameworks (by PXRD pattern), their chemical stabilities were drastically changed by the positional control of the \(\mathsf{C F}_{3}\) groups. In the case of UiO-67- ortho- \(2\mathrm{CF}_{3}\) , the hydrophobic trifluoromethyl group was placed near the site where the carboxylate coordinates to the zirconium, which protected it from nucleophilic attack. Contrastingly, the para- \(\mathsf{C F}_{3}\) functionalization could not protect the coordination structure. Therefore, UiO-67-ortho- \(2\mathrm{CF}_{3}\) was totally retained after treatments with boiling water, a strong acid (8 M aqueous HCl), and 50 ppm NaF solution. The structure also held up under basic conditions ( \(10\,\mathrm{mM}\) aqueous NaOH). Both NaOH and NaF conditions are widely utilized to digest and dissolve Zr-based MOFs for NMR confirmations. In addition, this strategy was successfully applied to two other useful MOF systems, DUT (DUT = Dresden University of Technology) and Al-TPDC (TPDC = para-terphenyl- \(\cdot4{,}4^{\prime\prime}\) -dicar boxylic acid). This study clearly displayed the importance and impact of functional group position in MOF structures. The detailed and careful design of functionalized ligands is highly important for MOF properties and their related applications.

