# 2.6. Halogen functionalities

Mono-halogenated ligands, such as BDC-F, BDC-Cl, BDC-Br, and BDC-I, have been widely utilized in MOF preparations. Tetrafluorofunctionalized ligands (e.g., BDC- \(\cdot\mathrm{F}_{4}\) ) have also been employed for several MOF formations since they are commercially available from multiple companies. Therefore, this section discusses the

intentional design and synthesis of halogen functionalities in MOFs with regioisomerism, as well as the methods used for controlling the number of functionalities introduced.

